cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  engine_simulator: Zero- and Quasi-Dimensional HCCI Engine
  Cycle Simulation in Python
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software
  and the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shingne
    given-names: Prasad S.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4885-6062"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prasadshingne/engine_simulator"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python package for zero-dimensional
  single-zone and quasi-dimensional multi-zone Homogeneous
  Charge Compression Ignition (HCCI) engine cycle
  simulation. Couples Cantera chemical kinetics with a
  temperature-stratified zone decomposition under a
  pressure-relaxation coupling, the Woschni heat transfer
  correlation, and an Adiabatic Core phenomenological model
  for fast combustion phasing estimates. Includes a
  Streamlit interface and tutorial notebooks.
keywords:
  - HCCI
  - engine simulation
  - combustion
  - chemical kinetics
  - multi-zone model
  - thermal stratification
  - Cantera
  - Python
